On my 5.1B ES40 system, this command works

mount -r /dev/disk/cdrom0c /cdrom

You might try being explicit about the cd format,
although I haven't found it to be necessary:

If the CD is in ISO9660 format:
mount -r -t cdfs /dev/disk/cdrom0c /cdrom

Or if the cd is in UFS format:
mount -r -t ufs  /dev/disk/cdrom0c /cdrom

Partition "c" is the entire disk, which is appropriate for CDROMs.

-jc
