> these machines do not reboot automatically & produce core files & how to
> force this behaviour/functionality? Thanks. Rakesh

Need some more details to determine why your systems do not create
core dumps. You should supply some details on your storage
configuration / swapdevice config.

You should check the following requirements for a proper working
crashdumpmechanism if you have a fiber optic based disk config:
1) MINIMUM of 1.25 -2 times physical memory for swap space.
2) ALL BOOT and SWAP devices properly configured and defined          
       as one of 4 "console devices" (in case of fiber based storage
configuration)
3) All wwidmgr configurations and settings properly set up for ALL
wid#'s and port#'s for ALL boot and swap devices at the console via
wwidmgr !As verified via hwmgr and consvar on the running system(s).
4) Ensure there is sufficient disk space to save the crash dumps on
the system. {i.e /var/adm/crash} ...

To make sure your system automatically restarts after a crash you
should set the console variable "auto_action". In your case it will
have the value "halt". To automatically restart you should give it the
value "restart" or "boot".


