One problem I had was that NIS passwd file exported the user's shell as
/usr/local/bin/tcsh and this shell was not present at this location on a
particular machine. A symlink could fix this. Look also at /etc/shells
file (some OSs have it, some don't). Also, if you are automounting the
home directories off some other box, it might be that your automounter
is not running, although in general in this case you should still be
logged in only with a defaultme directory being '/'

Ognen


