Gert-Jan Hilbrands wrote:

> To make sure your system automatically restarts after a crash you
> should set the console variable "auto_action". In your case it will
> have the value "halt". To automatically restart you should give it the
> value "restart" or "boot".

I would add that the "auto_action" variable should contain the value 
"restart", and not "boot".

The "auto_action" variable is consulted by the console code to determine a 
course of action when the console is entered without some instructions from 
the operating system.  There are many cases where the console is entered 
without instructions from the operating system.  The most common case is at 
power-up, but there are others, including "machine check while in PAL 
mode".   If the "auto_action" variable is set to "boot", then the console 
will simply reboot the operating system without attempting to notify the 
operating system of why it was rebooted.  If the "auto_action" variable is 
set to "restart", then if the console is entered, it will call a routine in 
the operating system still in memory to restart it.  If it fails to 
restart, then the console will boot the machine.

-- 

        Stu


