A backup of a running system will not normally cause any problems, although
it is allways better to have a 'cold' backup to fall back on. Sometimes
it is better/quicker to simply re-install and then apply your customisations
on top.
One thing that you may wish to consider is that there can be problems with
recovering your backups onto different hardware in a disaster.
I would strongly advise you to use AdVFS and Vdump for system level backups,
but for data backups I would suggest you use an enterprise backup product.
Remember if this system is so important that you cannot tolerate downtime
for a backup that it is obviously critical to the buisness and so backups
are extremely important. This means you must make sure that you perform
regular recovery tests. Make sure that you can recover the entire system
in a reasonable amount of time.
Hope this helps some
Adam Price
