 Lothar Esser <lesser@helix.nih.gov> wrote:

X Hi,
X  we are trying to connect a raid array with 1.4 TB to our ES40 Tru64
X v5.1.
X When we try to use diskconfig to partition and format the virtual disk
X we run
X into the problem that apparently the Gui has exceeded its limits. We get
X negative values
X for partition end and size (-952488.000). As a result of this it does
X not allow us to
X partition and format the disk and the gui is more or less frozen.
X Disk attributes are as follows:
X Physical Location bus-0-targ-1-lun-0   Sector/unit -195069542
X Bytes/sector 512    rpm: 5410
X :::
X sectors/cylinders 16384
X cylinders 12011
X 
X Well the question is -- now that I got spoiled with those guis, how can
X I
X partition the disk properly with disklabel and newfs ?
X Or is there an updated version of diskconfig ?
X 
X Thanks,
X Lothar
X 

Do not use a volume larger than 1TB or you will run into a lot more than 
diskconfig negative errors.  In v5.1 there is too much code that does 
the wrong thing for volumes greater than 1TB.  I do not think you can 
use greater than 1TB until v5.1b

UFS is not prepared to build a file system on a volume larger than 1TB.  
I do not think it can do that even in a v5.1b system, but I am not as 
sure of myself on that.

If you need a file system that is larger than 1TB, use AdvFS and 
multiple AdvFS volumes with each volume being 1TB or less.  Using 
multipe volumes AdvFS can create a 256TB domain.

(1,099,511,627,264 = (2^31 * 512) - 512).  Anything larger may result in 
corrupted data on a v5.1 system.

                                        Bob Harris


